## Layer 1: mechanical checks

No new user archive was supplied. `provenance/engine_comparison.json` hashes every engine and confirms identity with v052. The decisive PLAN.json binds all scientific Python sources and four paired JSON/NPZ v044 endpoint anchors. Pilot and primary records are stored separately. Primary checkpoint digests and contiguity are verified before publication; the production stop/resume check additionally preserves the first three states byte-for-byte.

The numerical driver reads local anchors/models and writes local checkpoint directories and logs. No network call, subprocess or deletion is added to the scientific driver. It performs authorized numerical model evaluation; it is not an inspection-only scanner run. No new dependency/CVE certification is claimed.

## Layer 2: deep-read cutoff

Reviewed in depth: the preparation schedule/driver, inherited loop and basis-transport integration, new endpoint frame join, acceptance validator, report generator and new tests. The unchanged sampler/spatial helper was checked for its current use. Unchanged Hamiltonian engines and unrelated historical drivers were not reread in full.

The endpoint join is the primary new risk: a root match alone does not determine a frame match. It validates the old frame file's digest and basis, handles root permutation, tests both two-planes, checks the charge transformation under each orientation sign, and accepts only a common relative orientation. It deliberately allows a common overall reflection. Coarse and fine parameter frames are saved and restored separately.

